From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] SystemUI recents: clear all shown whenever there are tasks

0024 puts the newest six tasks on one screen of icon cards that never scrolls,
"between the status bar and the clear-all button", and leaves the older tasks
to clear all. But the low ram layout shows that button only when the user
scrolls up to older tasks or dismisses a task: on the device it was missing
(Test V45, 25 recent tasks, six shown), so the other 19 could not be removed
from the screen until a card had been closed first.

With icon cards the button now follows the grid layout's rule: shown whenever
the stack has tasks, hidden when it has none: a static outlined button at the
bottom (0024), shown from the first layout instead of after a gesture.

--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/recents/views/TaskStackView.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/recents/views/TaskStackView.java
@@ -2408,6 +2408,18 @@
     }
 
     private void updateStackActionButtonVisibility() {
+        // PW3: icon cards do not scroll (TaskStackLowRamLayoutAlgorithm), so clear all is shown
+        // whenever there are tasks, as in grid layout. The low ram layout shows it only once the
+        // user scrolls up or dismisses a task: with six cards that never scroll it stayed hidden
+        // until a card was closed, and the older tasks could not be removed (Test V45).
+        if (Recents.getConfiguration().iconCards) {
+            if (mStack.getTaskCount() > 0) {
+                EventBus.getDefault().send(new ShowStackActionButtonEvent(false /* translate */));
+            } else {
+                EventBus.getDefault().send(new HideStackActionButtonEvent());
+            }
+            return;
+        }
         if (Recents.getConfiguration().isLowRamDevice) {
             return;
         }
